<title>EGYPT: Afreximbank helps finance Mauritanian oil imports.</title>
<headline>Afreximbank helps finance Mauritanian oil imports.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cairo-based African Export-Import Bank has agreed to provide the Mauritanian central bank with a revolving line of credit of $10 million to finance imports of oil from Algeria, the bank said on Friday.</p>
<p>The Banque Centrale de Mauritanie will use the money to open letters of credit for major Mauritanian petroleum distributors such as Naftec, Mobil, Elf and Somagaz, a statement said.</p>
<p>The credit is expected to rotate about four times a year, covering oil imports worth $40 million a year -- 85 percent of the country's total oil bill, it added.</p>
<p>&quot;(This) will ensure that GDP (gross domestic product) growth is sustained at about five percent annually in the near term, as targeted by the Mauritanian authorities,&quot; bank president Christopher Edordu told the signing ceremony.</p>
<p>An agreement on the credit was signed in Cairo on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
